28
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.600
Removing nullable A occurrences from

29
00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:55.960
A S A adds S

30
00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:57.820
A and A S, as

31
00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.760
well as the unit rule

32
00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.880
S becomes S.

33
00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.860
The old S is not

34
00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.580
nullable, because every terminating derivation

35
00:01:04.580 --> 00:01:06.240
still produces at least one

36
00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.320
a. Therefore this example does

37
00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.080
not acquire an empty-word rule

38
00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:11.520
